.1. "},{"tag":"b","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"b"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" GSE48261: EN weight vs. absolute value of effect size with l1 ratio = 0.9 and (top) alpha = 0.01 (middle) alpha = 0.05 (bottom) alpha = 0.1. "},{"tag":"b","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"c"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" GSE72774: EN weight vs. absolute value of effect size with l1 ratio = 0.5 and (top) alpha = 0.01 (middle) alpha = 0.05 (bottom) alpha = 0.1 (TIF 18.3 MB)"}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","hidden":false,"id":"MOESM9","attributes":{"class":"c-article-supplementary__item","data-test":"supp-item"},"children":[{"tag":"h3","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"},"children":[{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"attributes":{"data-test":"supp-info-link","class":"print-link","data-track":"call_to_action","data-track-action":"view supplementary info","data-track-context":"Supplementary Information","data-track-label":"11357_2024_1460_moesm9_esm.png","href":"https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11357-024-01460-1/MediaObjects/11357_2024_1460_MOESM9_ESM.png","data-supp-info-image":""},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"11357_2024_1460_MOESM9_ESM.png (download PNG "},{"tag":"#text","text":")"}]}]},{"tag":"div","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"c-article-supplementary__description","data-component":"thumbnail-container"},"children":[{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Supplementary file9"},{"tag":"b","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"a"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" (top) Histograms and fitted normal distributions of the residuals of the age predictions on the healthy cohort of the composite test dataset. (bottom) Q-Q plots for each model showing the goodness-of-fit of the normal distribution to the residuals. "},{"tag":"b","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"b"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" 10-year age bins of the residuals for the healthy cohort of the composite test dataset for each of the tested models (PNG 348 KB)"}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","hidden":false,"id":"MOESM10","attributes":{"class":"c-article-supplementary__item","data-test":"supp-item"},"children":[{"tag":"h3","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"},"children":[{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"attributes":{"data-test":"supp-info-link","class":"print-link","data-track":"call_to_action","data-track-action":"view supplementary info","data-track-context":"Supplementary Information","data-track-label":"11357_2024_1460_moesm10_esm.png","href":"https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11357-024-01460-1/MediaObjects/11357_2024_1460_MOESM10_ESM.png","data-supp-info-image":""},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"11357_2024_1460_MOESM10_ESM.png (download PNG "},{"tag":"#text","text":")"}]}]},{"tag":"div","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"c-article-supplementary__description","data-component":"thumbnail-container"},"children":[{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Supplementary file10"},{"tag":"b","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"a"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" Beta value versus age plotted for healthy controls (blue) and rheumatoid Arthritis patients (red) for representative CpGs in the GSE42861 dataset. (Top) A CpG for which the best-fit line for the RA cohort is shifted up from the HC cohort. (Bottom) A CpG for which the best-fit line for the RA cohort is down-shifted relative to the HC cohort. "},{"tag":"b","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"b"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" Table summary of how the product of the weights and disease shifts for model probes combines to produce either coherent or de-coherent feature shifts. "},{"tag":"b","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"c"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" Demonstration of the reflection transformation of the beta values for feature shift rectification (toy data). "},{"tag":"b","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"d"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" (Top row) Visualization of how the linear combination (weights times beta values) of both coherent and de-coherent feature shifts produces an incoherent picture of biological age-acceleration in the presence of disease. (Bottom) Visualization of how a linear combination of the rectified feature shifts (positive weights, reflected beta values for CpGs downshifted for a disease) produce a coherent image of the biological age acceleration due to disease (PNG 1.86 MB)"}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","hidden":false,"id":"MOESM11","attributes":{"class":"c-article-supplementary__item","data-test":"supp-item"},"children":[{"tag":"h3","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"},"children":[{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"attributes":{"data-test":"supp-info-link","class":"print-link","data-track":"call_to_action","data-track-action":"view supplementary info","data-track-context":"Supplementary Information","data-track-label":"11357_2024_1460_moesm11_esm.png","href":"https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11357-024-01460-1/MediaObjects/11357_2024_1460_MOESM11_ESM.png","data-supp-info-image":""},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"11357_2024_1460_MOESM11_ESM.png (download PNG "},{"tag":"#text","text":")"}]}]},{"tag":"div","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"c-article-supplementary__description","data-component":"thumbnail-container"},"children":[{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Supplementary file11"},{"tag":"b","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"a"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" (top) Correlation vs. number of features for RA coherent mFSS model trained on features ranked by age correlation. (bottom) Corresponding plot for MSE vs. number of features. Red dashed line indicates number of features which give the optimum validation MSE. "},{"tag":"b","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"b"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" (Left) scatter plot for predicted age vs. actual age for GSE72774. (right) box plot of the residuals of the predictions. "},{"tag":"b","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"c"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" (Left) scatter plot for predicted age vs. actual age for GSE125105. (right) box plot of the residuals of the predictions. "},{"tag":"b","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"d"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" (Left) scatter plot for predicted age vs. actual age for GSE53740. (right) box plot of the residuals of the predictions. "},{"tag":"b","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"e"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" (Left) scatter plot for predicted age vs. actual age for GSE53740. (right) box plot of the residuals of the predictions (PNG 616 KB)"}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","hidden":false,"id":"MOESM12","attributes":{"class":"c-article-supplementary__item","data-test":"supp-item"},"children":[{"tag":"h3","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"c-article-supplementary__title u-h3"},"children":[{"tag":"a","hidden":false,"attributes":{"data-test":"supp-info-link","class":"print-link","data-track":"call_to_action","data-track-action":"view supplementary info","data-track-context":"Supplementary Information","data-track-label":"11357_2024_1460_moesm12_esm.png","href":"https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1007%2Fs11357-024-01460-1/MediaObjects/11357_2024_1460_MOESM12_ESM.png","data-supp-info-image":""},"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"11357_2024_1460_MOESM12_ESM.png (download PNG "},{"tag":"#text","text":")"}]}]},{"tag":"div","hidden":false,"attributes":{"class":"c-article-supplementary__description","data-component":"thumbnail-container"},"children":[{"tag":"p","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"Supplementary file12"},{"tag":"b","hidden":false,"children":[{"tag":"#text","text":"a"}]},{"tag":"#text","text":" (top) Correlation vs. number of features for RA-coherent mFSS model trained on fea